-- title:
--   Eichler–Shimura representation as a quotient of Tₚ(J₀(N))
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$, a level $N\ge 1$ and a finite set $S\subseteq\mathbb N$ with $p\in S$ and containing every prime divisor of $N$. Let $\mathcal O'$ be a characteristic-zero complete (adically complete for its maximal ideal) discrete valuation domain with finite residue field in which $p$ lies in the maximal ideal, and let $\chi$ be a ring homomorphism to $\mathcal O'$ from [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 ↑S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18), the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb C}S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S$, together with the $U_q$ for primes $q\mid N$, $q\notin S$. The assertion is that there is a type $\mathcal O''$ carrying the same list of structures (characteristic-zero complete discrete valuation domain, finite residue field), an $\mathcal O'$-algebra structure making it a finite $\mathcal O'$-module with local and injective structure map, and a $\mathbb Z_p$-algebra structure, together with $\rho\in$ [`GaloisRepAdic 𝒪''`](def/GaloisRep_Adic.html#L16) — a free $\mathcal O''$-module $V$ of rank $2$ with an adically continuous monoid homomorphism $\rho.\rho$ from $\operatorname{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)=(\overline{\mathbb Q}\simeq_{\text{alg}[\mathbb Q]}\overline{\mathbb Q})$ to $\operatorname{End}_{\mathcal O''}V$ — such that: (1) for every prime $\ell\nmid N$ with $\ell\notin S$, every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\ell$ a non-unit of $A$, and every $\sigma$ lying in the decomposition subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb Q$ and acting on the residue field of $A$ by $x\mapsto x^{\ell}$, the characteristic polynomial of $\rho.\rho(\sigma)$ is $X^2-\chi(T_\ell)X+\ell$, the Hecke eigenvalue taken in $\mathcal O''$; (2) for every prime $q\nmid N$ with $q\neq p$ and every valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ in which $q$ is a non-unit, $\rho.\rho$ is trivial on the image of the corresponding inertia subgroup; (3) there are a fraction field $K_0$ of $\mathcal O''$ with compatible $\mathbb Z_p$-algebra structure and a surjective $K_0$-linear map $\pi\colon K_0\otimes_{\mathbb Z_p}T_p(J_0(N))\to K_0\otimes_{\mathcal O''}V$ intertwining, for every $\sigma$, the base change of the Galois action on the $p$-adic Tate module of $J_0(N)$ with the base change of $\rho.\rho(\sigma)$. Here $T_p(M)$ is the group of sequences $(x_n)$ in $M$ with $p^nx_n=0$ and $px_{n+1}=x_n$, and $J_0(N)$ is realised as the degree-zero divisor class group of the modular function field of level $N$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$.
--
--   This is the Eichler–Shimura–Deligne construction of the $p$-adic Galois representation attached to a homomorphism from the weight-two Hecke algebra of level $N$, in the form that also records the geometric provenance of the representation: $\rho$ becomes, after passage to the fraction field, a Galois-equivariant quotient of the $p$-adic Tate module of the Jacobian $J_0(N)$. The quotient presentation in clause (3) is what allows local behaviour at primes dividing the level to be read off from the Tate module, and is used in the analysis of inertia at such primes for newforms.
